                    "text": "Agent: explore\nDescription: 查找跳跃状态机实现\nDurationMs: 52065\nTotalTokens: 135K\n\nOutput:\nHere is a comprehensive summary of all findings.\n\n---\n\n## 1. `Jump_fsm` is **not** a separate class — it is an instance of `Class_FSM`\n\n`Jump_fsm` is declared as a **public member variable** of `Class_DOG` in:\n\n**File:** `Development_Layer/Function_Class/Class_RobotDog/robotdog_class.h` (line 37)\n```cpp\nclass Class_DOG{\npublic:\n    // ...\n    Class_FSM Jump_fsm;    // <--- this is the instance\n    // ...\n};\n```\n\nSo `Jump_fsm` uses the generic `Class_FSM` state machine class defined and implemented in:\n\n- **Header:** `Development_Layer/Function_Class/Class_FSM/fsm_class.h`\n- **Source:** `Development_Layer/Function_Class/Class_FSM/fsm_class.cpp`\n\n---\n\n## 2. `Init` Method Signature\n\n**Declaration** (fsm_class.h, line 48):\n```cpp\nvoid Init(uint8_t __Status_Number, uint8_t __Now_Status_Serial = 0);\n```\n\n**Implementation** (fsm_class.cpp, lines 12–27):\n```cpp\nvoid Class_FSM::Init(uint8_t __Status_Number, uint8_t __Now_Status_Serial)\n{\n    Status_Number = __Status_Number;\n    Now_Status_Serial = __Now_Status_Serial;\n\n    // 所有状态全刷0\n    for (int i = 0; i < Status_Number; i++)\n    {\n        Status[i].Status_Stage = Status_Stage_DISABLE;\n        Status[i].Count_Time = 0;\n    }\n\n    // 使能初始状态\n    Status[__Now_Status_Serial].Status_Stage = Status_Stage_ENABLE;\n}\n```\n\n| Parameter | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `__Status_Number` | Total number of states in the FSM. This determines how many entries in the `Status[]` array are used (up to `STATUS_MAX = 10`). |\n| `__Now_Status_Serial` | **Initial state index** (defaults to `0`). The state at this index is immediately set to `ENABLE`; all others are `DISABLE`. |\n\n**Concrete usage** in `callback_task.cpp` (line 24):\n```cpp\ndog.Jump_fsm.Init(4, 0);   // 4 states total, initial state = 0\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. `Set_Status` Method\n\n**Declaration and inline implementation** (fsm_class.h, lines 52/97–106):\n```cpp\ninline void Class_FSM::Set_Status(uint8_t Next_Status_serial)\n{\n    // 失能当前状态, 计数器清零\n    Status[Now_Status_Serial].Status_Stage = Status_Stage_DISABLE;\n    Status[Now_Status_Serial].Count_Time = 0;\n\n    // 转到下一个状态\n    Status[Next_Status_serial].Status_Stage = Status_Stage_ENABLE;\n    Now_Status_Serial = Next_Status_serial;\n}\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n1. **Disables** the current active state (writes `DISABLE` to its `Status_Stage` and **resets its `Count_Time` to 0**).\n2. **Enables** the destination state (`Next_Status_serial`) by setting its `Status_Stage` to `ENABLE`.\n3. Updates `Now_Status_Serial` to the new state index.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `Get_Now_Status_Serial` Method\n\n**Inline getter** (fsm_class.h, lines 50/87–90):\n```cpp\ninline uint8_t Class_FSM::Get_Now_Status_Serial()\n{\n    return (Now_Status_Serial);\n}\n```\n\nSimply returns the `uint8_t` index of the currently active state.\n\n---\n\n## 5. The `Status` Array and `Count_Time` Member\n\nDefined in `fsm_class.h` (lines 32–36, 46):\n```cpp\n#define STATUS_MAX (10)\n\nenum Enum_Status_Stage\n{\n    Status_Stage_DISABLE = 0,\n    Status_Stage_ENABLE,\n};\n\nstruct Struct_Status\n{\n    Enum_Status_Stage Status_Stage;   // DISABLE (0) or ENABLE (1)\n    uint32_t Count_Time;              // elapsed tick counter\n};\n\nclass Class_FSM\n{\npublic:\n    Struct_Status Status[STATUS_MAX];  // fixed-size array of 10 status slots\n    // ...\nprotected:\n    uint8_t Status_Number;             // how many states are actually used (up to 10)\n    uint8_t Now_Status_Serial;         // current active state index\n};\n```\n\n| Member | Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Status[STATUS_MAX]` | `Struct_Status[10]` | Array of state slots. Each slot has a stage (enabled/disabled) and a tick counter. |\n| `Status[i].Status_Stage` | `Enum_Status_Stage` | Whether state `i` is currently enabled (`ENABLE`) or disabled (`DISABLE`). |\n| `Status[i].Count_Time` | `uint32_t` | Accumulated tick count for state `i`. Incremented while that state is active; **reset to 0 on state entry**. |\n| `Status_Number` | `uint8_t` | How many states are defined (set by `Init`). Only indices `0..Status_Number-1` are iterated in initialization. |\n| `Now_Status_Serial` | `uint8_t` | Index of the currently active (enabled) state. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. How the State Machine Handles Timers Internally\n\nThere are two timer callback methods (both are templates meant to be overridden/used by subclasses):\n\n**In `fsm_class.cpp` (lines 34–51):**\n```cpp\nvoid Class_FSM::RTOS_Calculate_Callback()\n{\n    Status[Now_Status_Serial].Count_Time++;\n    // 自己接着编写状态转移函数\n}\n\nvoid Class_FSM::TIM_Calculate_PeriodElapsedCallback()\n{\n    Status[Now_Status_Serial].Count_Time++;\n    // 自己接着编写状态转移函数\n}\n```\n\n**The tick mechanism works as follows:**\n\n1. **A periodic timer** (in this project, `TIM6` fires every **1 ms**) calls one of these callbacks.\n2. The callback **increments `Count_Time`** for the **currently active state only** (`Status[Now_Status_Serial].Count_Time++`). Inactive states' counters do not increment.\n3. The user is expected to add custom transition logic after the `Count_Time++` line (inlined in the call site in this project, not in the class itself — see below).\n\n**In this project** (`callback_task.cpp`, line 61), the actual usage pattern is:\n```cpp\nvoid Tim6_Robot_1ms_Callback()\n{\n    robot_1ms_cycle_flag = true;\n    // ...\n    dog.Jump_fsm.TIM_Calculate_PeriodElapsedCallback();  // ticks the active state's Count_Time\n    dog.Chassis_Control();\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nThen the transition logic lives directly in the main loop (lines 65–172), using **timeout-based transitions**:\n```cpp\n// State 0: 起跳部分 (takeoff)\nif (dog.Jump_fsm.Status[0].Count_Time > 500)   // wait 500ms\n{\n    dog.Jump_fsm.Set_Status(1);                 // → state 1\n}\n\n// State 1: 收腿部分 (tuck legs)\nif (dog.Jump_fsm.Status[1].Count_Time > 700)   // wait 700ms\n{\n    dog.Jump_fsm.Set_Status(2);                 // → state 2\n}\n\n// State 2: 落地缓冲 (landing buffer)\nif (dog.Jump_fsm.Status[2].Count_Time > 1500)  // wait 1500ms\n{\n    dog.Jump_fsm.Set_Status(3);                 // → state 3 (idle)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of the Timer Lifecycle\n\n| Event | What happens |\n|---|---|\n| **`Init(4, 0)`** | All 4 states get `Status_Stage=DISABLE, Count_Time=0`. State 0 gets `ENABLE`. |\n| **`Set_Status(N)`** | Current state's `Count_Time` reset to 0 and stage set to `DISABLE`. New state `N` gets `ENABLE`. |\n| **Every 1ms tick** (`TIM_Calculate_PeriodElapsedCallback`) | `Status[Now_Status_Serial].Count_Time++` — only the active state's counter ticks up. |\n| **Application logic checks** | `Status[i].Count_Time > threshold` → calls `Set_Status(next)` to transition. |"
